# 37. Key Takeaway

The most important concept from today's lesson is that Linux commands are designed to work together.

For example:

    command1 | command2 | command3

The general flow is:

    Input
      |
      v
    Command 1
      |
    stdout
      |
      v
    Command 2
      |
    stdout
      |
      v
    Command 3
      |
      v
    Output

This command-line philosophy makes Linux extremely powerful.

These concepts will be useful for:

- Linux administration
- Shell scripting
- Networking
- Cybersecurity
- Digital forensics
- Log analysis
- CTF challenges
